  "verdict": "No regression was measured on the supported AC20 and ISSUE_129 fixtures. The heavy Holter result is inconclusive and cannot exclude a small overhead: its pooled full-wall median was 1.75% slower and three of four adjacent paired medians favored base, while sample spread remained too wide for a confident regression verdict. Every geometry fingerprint and entity/mesh/triangle count matched. This is a native full-load verdict only and makes no browser worker-pool or UI speedup claim.",
  "method": {
    "command": "perf_probe <fixture> --iters 5 --fingerprint --json",
    "buildCommand": "cargo build --locked --profile profiling -p ifc-lite-processing --example perf_probe",
    "cargoFeatures": "default; no explicit --features",
    "rustFlags": "repository profiling profile; no additional RUSTFLAGS supplied",
    "invocationOrder": [
      "base",
      "branch",
      "branch",
      "base",
      "branch",
      "base",
      "base",
      "branch"
    ],
    "invocationOrderDescription": "Two balanced blocks: ABBA followed by BAAB. Adjacent entries are analyzed as four base/branch pairs.",
    "samplesPerRevisionPerFixture": 20,
    "preparatoryWork": "Default perf_probe mode performs three isolated entity-index scans before each invocation's five full-pipeline samples. These scans warm the source bytes but are not full process_geometry warmups.",
    "isolation": "The two profiling executables were built once from pinned worktrees, hashed, and invoked directly without rebuilding. Measurements ran after compilation/testing activity had stopped. Every process used RAYON_NUM_THREADS=12, processor affinity 0x000FFF, High priority, and the Windows High performance power scheme.",
    "affinityCaveat": "PowerShell applies ProcessorAffinity and PriorityClass immediately after Start-Process returns; a small startup interval precedes those assignments.",
    "metricNotes": "parseMs, geometryMs, and totalMs describe the minimum-total iteration selected by perf_probe. ProcessingStats records those fields with Duration::as_millis(), so allTotalsMs has integer-millisecond truncation: AC20's 13 ms versus 14 ms pooled medians differ by one truncated tick. allTotalsMs and allWallMs retain all samples, and pooled and adjacent-pair medians below use those complete arrays. AC20's paired wall results are mixed, and varianceRule intentionally defines no numeric spread threshold; the pooled percentages are therefore not standalone regression evidence. The ordered FNV-1a64 fingerprint covers ordered geometry payload identity; it excludes metadata, UVs, textures, and instancing.",
    "sourceHashScope": "The measured source hashes cover production files linked into perf_probe. Test-only sources and later documentation-only changes are excluded.",
    "varianceRule": "A wide spread or consistently one-sided paired result is reported as inconclusive rather than converted into a no-regression claim."
  },
